# pipeline-ui's own settings, read by bin/pipeline after the pipeline's secrets file
# (PIPELINE_ENV), so a value here wins; the service loads the file itself too (server/config.ts),
# and a variable already in the environment wins over the file. Copy to .env (gitignored) on
# each machine; never commit .env. Every value is checked at start: a bad one stops the service
# with every problem named.
#
# Jira, for a queued ticket's summary, the console's ticket search and the tickets' statuses on
# the statistics page. A scoped Atlassian API token: Jira takes it only through
# api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/<cloudId>. All three are needed; the console links a ticket key to
# JIRA_BASE_URL/browse/KEY. JIRA_BASE_URL is the site with its scheme, such as
# https://your-site.atlassian.net.
JIRA_BASE_URL=
JIRA_EMAIL=
JIRA_API_TOKEN=
# Optional: the site's cloud id (read from the site's /_edge/tenant_info when unset).
# JIRA_CLOUD_ID=
#
# Bitbucket, for the pull requests' states; usually in the pipeline's secrets file already.
# BITBUCKET_TOKEN=
#
# Not secrets, but per machine too: the branch a run starts from and its pull request goes to
# (default master; it must have the entry point, so dev while webui's master does not), and
# whether a run may push and open its pull request (default on; off for a machine's first runs;
# draft to open every pull request as a draft). These two and the hours below are the defaults
# of the run settings: the console's settings (the gear in the masthead) change them for the next run without a restart.
# PIPELINE_BASE_BRANCH=dev
# PIPELINE_PULL_REQUESTS=off
#
# Where things are (defaults: the webui checkout next to this repository, ./data, the pipeline's
# secrets file at ~/.config/webui-pipeline.env, one session at most 4 hours).
# PIPELINE_WEBUI=../webui
# PIPELINE_DATA=./data
# PIPELINE_ENV=~/.config/webui-pipeline.env
# PIPELINE_TIMEOUT_HOURS=4
#
# The console's address (default 0.0.0.0, all interfaces, port 8787). On a server, keep the port
# behind a firewall or set 127.0.0.1 and open it through an SSH tunnel.
# PIPELINE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PIPELINE_PORT=8787
#
# The tools' start page: set, the mark in the masthead leads to it, as every tool's logo does.
# PIPELINE_PORTAL_URL=http://tools.example.net/
#
# The console's guard (server/http/guard.ts). It answers only to a Host it knows: an IP address,
# localhost, this machine's name, or one of these names (comma separated), so a page on another
# site cannot reach it by a name it does not expect.
# PIPELINE_HOSTNAMES=pipeline.example.net
# Both set, every page but /healthz asks for this login (HTTP basic auth); neither set, none.
# PIPELINE_USER=
# PIPELINE_PASSWORD=
#
# `pipeline maintain` (daily from deploy/pipeline-ui-maintain.timer): where the database's
# backups go (the latest 14 kept; default <data>/backups) and the service's log file as the
# unit appends it (cut down once past 5 MB; default <data>/serve.log).
# PIPELINE_BACKUP_DIR=
# PIPELINE_LOG_FILE=
